.TH NOTEPADLX 1 "2026-10-25" "NotePadLX 0.6" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
notepadlx \- source code editor, a Linux port of Notepad++
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B notepadlx
[\fIoptions\fR] [\fIfile\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
NotePadLX is a Qt 6 port of the Notepad++ text and source code editor. It uses the
Scintilla editing component and the Lexilla lexers, reads Notepad++ themes and configuration
files, and supports syntax highlighting, folding, Find in Files, macros and more.
.SH OPTIONS
The Notepad++ command line options are supported, for example:
.TP
.B \-multiInst
Start another instance instead of opening the files in the running one.
.TP
.B \-nosession
Do not restore the previous session and do not save it at exit.
.TP
.BI \-n line
Go to the given line.
.TP
.BI \-c column
Go to the given column.
.TP
.BI \-l language
Open the files with the given language, for example \fB\-lpython\fR.
.TP
.B \-ro
Open the files read-only.
.TP
.B \-openFoldersAsWorkspace
Open the given folders in the Folder as Workspace panel.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/notepadlx/
The user settings: config.xml, shortcuts.xml, stylers.xml, session.xml and the themes.
.TP
.I /usr/share/notepadlx/
The default settings, themes, languages and localization files.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NPLX_THEME
\fBlight\fR or \fBdark\fR overrides the interface theme.
.SH SEE ALSO
https://github.com/ClaudiuJitea/NotePadLX
